# /keycloak-verify — Keycloak app-auth verification

Confirms the auth model documented in **keycloak-app-auth** is actually applied to the
running Keycloak + the app code. Read-only except where you opt into `keycloak:apply`.

## Run order

```bash
# 1. Static server config (realm/client/group/mapper/redirect URIs).
#    Reads admin creds from $KC_USER/$KC_PASS or SSM. Read-only.
pnpm keycloak:doctor

# 2. App-side contract (token verification + admin authorization logic).
pnpm exec vitest run __tests__/api-auth.test.ts

# 3. If doctor reports drift, fix it idempotently, then re-verify:
pnpm keycloak:apply:dry      # preview
pnpm keycloak:apply          # apply
pnpm keycloak:doctor         # confirm green

# 4. (Optional) full login flow against production — needs e2e users:
E2E_BASE_URL=https://cloudless.gr pnpm e2e:prod
```

## What "correct" looks like

`pnpm keycloak:doctor` should print all PASS:

- OIDC discovery reachable, `issuer` == `KEYCLOAK_ISSUER`
- JWKS has ≥ 1 key
- `cloudless-app` is a **public** client with **PKCE S256**
- redirectUris include `https://cloudless.gr/api/auth/callback/keycloak`
- `admin` group exists
- group-membership mapper (`groups` claim) present on `cloudless-app`

`__tests__/api-auth.test.ts` should pass — it pins:
- signature verification against the JWKS when `KEYCLOAK_ISSUER` is set
- `isAdmin()` reads `groups` / `realm_access.roles` (legacy `cognito:groups` still honored)

## If something fails

| Failing check | Fix |
| --- | --- |
| discovery/JWKS unreachable | Keycloak pod down or DNS — see `keycloak-ops` (k3s `keycloak` ns) |
| client not public / no PKCE | `pnpm keycloak:apply` |
| redirect URI missing | `pnpm keycloak:apply` (or `keycloak.sh client-update-redirect`) |
| admin group / groups mapper missing | `pnpm keycloak:apply` |
| api-auth.test.ts red | the app-auth contract drifted — see **keycloak-app-auth** skill |

